IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg9, LAYER 1: Subchapter X, sections 278 to 285.
-- Continuation of a corporation after dissolution; trustees and receivers for a dissolved corporation; notice to
-- claimants; payment and distribution; liability of stockholders; jurisdiction; revocation or forfeiture of charter.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the
-- Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550). It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is
-- line N of that file (an ellipsis means the line goes on).
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view: each rule is the relation the text states between a dissolved
-- corporation or its successor entity, its claimants, its stockholders, its directors and the Court of Chancery.
-- A judgment the text hands to the Court or to the corporation is never guessed: it is a plain input.
-- Law outside the range is a plain input: the Rules of the Court of Chancery and section 114 and section 295
-- (the latter is in piece dg9 but in another module, dg9-xi-receivers).
--
-- Sections 271, 276, 311, 312 and 313 are listed in section 114(b)(1), and 274 and 275 in section 114(b)(2); sections
-- 278 to 285 are not, so the section 114(a) reading (stockholder as member) reaches them where it fits. Sections 280(g)
-- and 281(f) state their own rule for a nonprofit nonstock corporation.

§ `Subchapter X. Sale of Assets, Dissolution and Winding Up`

§§ `s 278 Continuation of corporation after dissolution for purposes of suit and winding up affairs`

-- "for the term of 3 years from such expiration or dissolution or for such longer period as the Court of Chancery
-- shall in its discretion direct".
-- src:1456 | for the term of 3 years from such expiration or dissolution or for such longer period as the Court of Chancery shall in its discretion direct, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 278 (src:1456)
`s 278 the term of continuation` MEANS `period in years` 3

-- The last day of the period: 3 years from the date of expiration or dissolution (the anniversary itself is inside,
-- fork F5 in NOTES.md), or the date the Court of Chancery has directed, if that is later. The Court's discretion is
-- a plain input and is never guessed.
-- src:1456 | All corporations, whether they expire by their own limitation or are otherwise dissolved, shall nevertheless be continued, for the term of 3 years from such expiration or dissolution or for such longer period as the Court of Chancery shall in its discretion direct, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 278 (src:1456)
GIVEN `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS A DATE
      `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the end of the 3 years`
    WHEN JUST directed THEN (IF directed GREATER THAN `the end of the 3 years` THEN directed ELSE `the end of the 3 years`)
    WHERE
        `the end of the 3 years` MEANS `the date` `s 278 the term of continuation` `after` `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved`

-- "for the purpose of prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against
-- them, and of enabling them gradually to settle and close their business, to dispose of and convey their
-- property, to discharge their liabilities and to distribute to their stockholders any remaining assets, but not for
-- the purpose of continuing the business for which the corporation was organized."
-- src:1456 | for the purpose of prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against them, and of enabling them gradually to settle and close their business, to dispose of and convey their property, to discharge their liabilities and to distribute to their stockholders any remaining assets, but not for the purpose of continuing the business for which the corporation was organized. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 278 (src:1456)
DECLARE `s 278 Purpose for which a corporation continues` IS ONE OF
    `prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against the corporation`
    `enabling the corporation gradually to settle and close its business`
    `disposing of and conveying its property`
    `discharging its liabilities`
    `distributing to its stockholders any remaining assets`
    `continuing the business for which the corporation was organized`

-- src:1456 | for the purpose of prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against them, and of enabling them gradually to settle and close their business, to dispose of and convey their property, to discharge their liabilities and to distribute to their stockholders any remaining assets, but not for the purpose of continuing the business for which the corporation was organized. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 278 (src:1456)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 278 Purpose for which a corporation continues`
      `the date of the question` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period of continuation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `continuing the business for which the corporation was organized` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the date of the question` AT MOST `the last day of the period of continuation`

-- "With respect to any action, suit or proceeding begun by or against the corporation either prior to or within 3
-- years after the date of its expiration or dissolution, the action shall not abate by reason of the dissolution of
-- the corporation; the corporation shall, solely for the purpose of such action, suit or proceeding, be continued as a
-- body corporate beyond the 3-year period and until any judgments, orders or decrees therein shall be fully
-- executed, without the necessity for any special direction to that effect by the Court of Chancery."
-- src:1456 | With respect to any action, suit or proceeding begun by or against the corporation either prior to or within 3 years after the date of its expiration or dissolution, the action shall not abate by reason of the dissolution of the corporation; the corporation shall, solely for the purpose of such action, suit or proceeding, be continued as a body corporate beyond the 3-year period and until any judgments, orders or decrees therein shall be fully executed, without the necessity for any special direction to that effect by the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 278 (src:1456)
GIVEN `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate, and the action does not abate, for the sake of the action, suit or proceeding` MEANS
        `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution`
    AND (NOT `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed`)

-- "Sections 279 through 282 of this title shall apply to any corporation that has expired by its own limitation, and
-- when so applied, all references in those sections to a dissolved corporation or dissolution shall include a
-- corporation that has expired by its own limitation and to such expiration, respectively."
-- src:1457 | Sections 279 through 282 of this title shall apply to any corporation that has expired by its own limitation, and when so applied, all references in those sections to a dissolved corporation or dissolution shall include a corporation that has expired by its own limitation and to such expiration, respectively.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 278 (src:1457)
GIVEN `the corporation has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has expired by its own limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 278 sections 279 to 282 apply to the corporation as a dissolved corporation` MEANS
    `the corporation has been dissolved` OR `the corporation has expired by its own limitation`

§§ `s 279 Trustees or receivers for dissolved corporations; appointment; powers; duties`

-- The Court of Chancery, "on application of any creditor, stockholder or director of the corporation, or any other
-- person who shows good cause therefor, at any time, may" appoint trustees or receivers for a corporation "dissolved
-- in any manner whatever". The applicant is a party of the core's cast: a creditor, a stockholder or a director needs
-- no showing; any other party must show good cause. The Court "may": the rule says only that the application is
-- one the Court may act on.
-- src:1461 | When any corporation organized under this chapter shall be dissolved in any manner whatever, the Court of Chancery, on application of any creditor, stockholder or director of the corporation, or any other person who shows good cause therefor, at any time, may either appoint …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 279 (src:1461)
GIVEN `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant` IS AN Actor
      `the applicant shows good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` MEANS
        `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever`
    AND (CONSIDER `the applicant`
         WHEN `a creditor` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a stockholder` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a director` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE `the applicant shows good cause`)

-- "appoint 1 or more of the directors of the corporation to be trustees, or appoint 1 or more persons to be receivers".
-- A trustee is one of the directors; a receiver is any person. For any other office the text says nothing.
-- src:1461 | either appoint 1 or more of the directors of the corporation to be trustees, or appoint 1 or more persons to be receivers, of and for the corporation, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 279 (src:1461)
GIVEN `the office` IS AN Actor
      `the appointee is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279 the person may be appointed to the office` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `a trustee` THEN JUST `the appointee is a director of the corporation`
    WHEN `a receiver` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1461 | to take charge of the corporation’s property, and to collect the debts and property due and belonging to the corporation, with power to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation, or otherwise, all such suits as may be necessary or proper for the purposes aforesaid, and to appoint an agent or agents under them, and to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation, if in being, that may be necessary for the final settlement of the unfinished business of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 279 (src:1461)
DECLARE `s 279 Power of a trustee or receiver` IS ONE OF
    `to take charge of the corporation's property`
    `to collect the debts and property due and belonging to the corporation`
    `to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all suits necessary or proper for those purposes`
    `to appoint an agent or agents under them`
    `to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation, if in being, that may be necessary for the final settlement of its unfinished business`

-- src:1461 | to take charge of the corporation’s property, and to collect the debts and property due and belonging to the corporation, with power to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation, or otherwise, all such suits as may be necessary or proper for the purposes aforesaid, and to appoint an agent or agents under them, and to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation, if in being, that may be necessary for the final settlement of the unfinished business of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 279 (src:1461)
`s 279 the powers of the trustees or receivers` MEANS
    LIST `to take charge of the corporation's property`
       , `to collect the debts and property due and belonging to the corporation`
       , `to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all suits necessary or proper for those purposes`
       , `to appoint an agent or agents under them`
       , `to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation, if in being, that may be necessary for the final settlement of its unfinished business`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 279 (src:1461)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `s 279 Power of a trustee or receiver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 279 the trustee or receiver has the power` MEANS
    elem `the power` `s 279 the powers of the trustees or receivers`

-- "The powers of the trustees or receivers may be continued as long as the Court of Chancery shall think necessary
-- for the purposes aforesaid."
-- src:1461 | The powers of the trustees or receivers may be continued as long as the Court of Chancery shall think necessary for the purposes aforesaid.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 279 (src:1461)
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery thinks the continuation of the powers necessary for the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 279 the powers of the trustees or receivers may be continued` MEANS
    `the Court of Chancery thinks the continuation of the powers necessary for the purposes`

§§ `s 280 Notice to claimants; filing of claims`

-- Paragraph (a)(1): the notice states (a.) that claims must be presented in writing with sufficient information
-- reasonably to inform of the claimant's identity and the substance of the claim; (b.) the mailing address; (c.) the
-- date by which a claim must be received, "no earlier than 60 days from the date thereof"; (d.) that the claim will be
-- barred if not received by that date; (e.) that the corporation or a successor entity may make distributions to
-- other claimants and the stockholders without further notice; and (f.) the aggregate annual amount of distributions
-- to stockholders for each of the 3 years before dissolution.
-- src:1465 | (a) (1) After a corporation has been dissolved in accordance with the procedures set forth in this chapter, the corporation or any successor entity may give notice of the dissolution, requiring all persons having a claim against the corporation other than a claim against the corporation in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party to present their claims against the corporation in accordance with such notice. Such notice shall state:
-- src:1466 | a. That all such claims must be presented in writing and must contain sufficient information reasonably to inform the corporation or successor entity of the identity of the claimant and the substance of the claim;
-- src:1467 | b. The mailing address to which such a claim must be sent;
-- src:1468 | c. The date by which such a claim must be received by the corporation or successor entity, which date shall be no earlier than 60 days from the date thereof; and
-- src:1469 | d. That such claim will be barred if not received by the date referred to in paragraph (a)(1)c. of this section; and
-- src:1470 | e. That the corporation or a successor entity may make distributions to other claimants and the corporation’s stockholders or persons interested as having been such without further notice to the claimant; and
-- src:1471 | f. The aggregate amount, on an annual basis, of all distributions made by the corporation to its stockholders for each of the 3 years prior to the date the corporation dissolved.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(1) (src:1465-1471)
DECLARE `s 280(a)(1) Notice to claimants` HAS
    `statement that claims must be presented in writing with sufficient information reasonably to inform of the identity of the claimant and the substance of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the mailing address to which a claim must be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the notice` IS A DATE
    `date by which a claim must be received` IS A DATE
    `statement that the claim will be barred if not received by that date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that distributions may be made to other claimants and the stockholders without further notice to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the aggregate amount, on an annual basis, of all distributions to stockholders for each of the 3 years before dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1468 | c. The date by which such a claim must be received by the corporation or successor entity, which date shall be no earlier than 60 days from the date thereof; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(1) (src:1468)
`s 280(a)(1) the least time allowed to present a claim` MEANS `period in days` 60

-- src:1465 | (a) (1) After a corporation has been dissolved in accordance with the procedures set forth in this chapter, the corporation or any successor entity may give notice of the dissolution, requiring all persons having a claim against the corporation other than a claim against the corporation in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party to present their claims against the corporation in accordance with such notice. Such notice shall state:
-- src:1466 | a. That all such claims must be presented in writing and must contain sufficient information reasonably to inform the corporation or successor entity of the identity of the claimant and the substance of the claim;
-- src:1467 | b. The mailing address to which such a claim must be sent;
-- src:1468 | c. The date by which such a claim must be received by the corporation or successor entity, which date shall be no earlier than 60 days from the date thereof; and
-- src:1469 | d. That such claim will be barred if not received by the date referred to in paragraph (a)(1)c. of this section; and
-- src:1470 | e. That the corporation or a successor entity may make distributions to other claimants and the corporation’s stockholders or persons interested as having been such without further notice to the claimant; and
-- src:1471 | f. The aggregate amount, on an annual basis, of all distributions made by the corporation to its stockholders for each of the 3 years prior to the date the corporation dissolved.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(1) (src:1465-1471)
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `s 280(a)(1) Notice to claimants`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` MEANS
        `the notice`'s `statement that claims must be presented in writing with sufficient information reasonably to inform of the identity of the claimant and the substance of the claim`
    AND `the notice`'s `statement of the mailing address to which a claim must be sent`
    AND ((`the notice`'s `date by which a claim must be received`) AT LEAST (`the date` `s 280(a)(1) the least time allowed to present a claim` `after` (`the notice`'s `date of the notice`)))
    AND `the notice`'s `statement that the claim will be barred if not received by that date`
    AND `the notice`'s `statement that distributions may be made to other claimants and the stockholders without further notice to the claimant`
    AND `the notice`'s `statement of the aggregate amount, on an annual basis, of all distributions to stockholders for each of the 3 years before dissolution`

-- Publication and mailing: "at least once a week for 2 consecutive weeks in a newspaper of general circulation in
-- the county in which the office of the corporation's last registered agent in this State is located and in the
-- corporation's principal place of business and, in the case of a corporation having $10,000,000 or more in total
-- assets at the time of its dissolution, at least once in all editions of a daily newspaper with a national
-- circulation. On or before the date of the first publication of such notice, the corporation or successor entity shall
-- mail a copy of such notice by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to each known claimant".
-- Reading taken (fork F6): publication in both places, not one newspaper that happens to serve both.
-- src:1472 | Such notice shall also be published at least once a week for 2 consecutive weeks in a newspaper of general circulation in the county in which the office of the corporation’s last registered agent in this State is located and in the corporation’s principal place of business and, in the case of a corporation having $10,000,000 or more in total assets at the time of its dissolution, at least once in all editions of a daily newspaper with a national circulation. On or before the date of the first publication of such notice, the corporation or successor entity shall mail a copy of such notice by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to each known claimant of the corporation including persons with claims asserted against the corporation in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(1) (src:1472)
`s 280(a)(1) the total assets from which a national daily newspaper is required` MEANS 10_000_000

@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(1) (src:1472)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive weeks in which the notice was published at least once a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice was published in a newspaper of general circulation in the county in which the office of the corporation's last registered agent in this State is located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was published in a newspaper of general circulation in the corporation's principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total assets of the corporation at the time of its dissolution, in dollars` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: total assets, as the Law's other chapters define them, are a plain figure
      `the notice was published at least once in all editions of a daily newspaper with a national circulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the first publication of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date a copy of the notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to each known claimant` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the copy was mailed to each known claimant including persons with claims asserted in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants was published and mailed as the paragraph requires` MEANS
        `the number of consecutive weeks in which the notice was published at least once a week` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the notice was published in a newspaper of general circulation in the county in which the office of the corporation's last registered agent in this State is located`
    AND `the notice was published in a newspaper of general circulation in the corporation's principal place of business`
    AND (    (`the total assets of the corporation at the time of its dissolution, in dollars` LESS THAN `s 280(a)(1) the total assets from which a national daily newspaper is required`)
         OR  `the notice was published at least once in all editions of a daily newspaper with a national circulation`)
    AND `the copy was mailed to each known claimant including persons with claims asserted in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date a copy of the notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to each known claimant`
         WHEN JUST mailed THEN mailed AT MOST `the date of the first publication of the notice`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

-- Paragraph (a)(2): "Any claim against the corporation required to be presented pursuant to this subsection is barred
-- if a claimant who was given actual notice under this subsection does not present the claim to the dissolved
-- corporation or successor entity by the date referred to in paragraph (a)(1)c."
-- src:1473 | (2) Any claim against the corporation required to be presented pursuant to this subsection is barred if a claimant who was given actual notice under this subsection does not present the claim to the dissolved corporation or successor entity by the date referred to in paragraph (a)(1)c. of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(2) (src:1473)
GIVEN `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(a)(2) the claim is barred for want of presentation` MEANS
        `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party`
    AND `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was`
         WHEN JUST presented THEN presented GREATER THAN `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)

-- Paragraph (a)(3): rejection "by mailing notice of such rejection by certified or registered mail, return receipt
-- requested, to the claimant within 90 days after receipt of such claim and, in all events, at least 150 days before
-- the expiration of the period described in § 278". Both limits apply (fork F7). Where the claim is filed under
-- section 295 against a corporation for which the Court of Chancery has appointed a receiver or trustee, "the time
-- period shall be as provided in § 296": section 296 (piece dg9, module dg9-xi-receivers) governs and this
-- paragraph's periods say nothing, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:1474 | (3) A corporation or successor entity may reject, in whole or in part, any claim made by a claimant pursuant to this subsection by mailing notice of such rejection by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to the claimant within 90 days after receipt of such claim and, in all events, at least 150 days before the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title; provided however, that in the case of a claim filed pursuant to § 295 of this title against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery the time period shall be as provided in § 296 of this title, and the 30-day appeal period provided for in § 296 of this title shall be applicable. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(3) (src:1474)
`s 280(a)(3) the longest time after receipt of a claim to mail the rejection` MEANS `period in days` 90

-- src:1474 | at least 150 days before the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title; provided however, that in the case of a claim filed pursuant to § 295 of this title against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery the time period shall be as provided in § 296 of this title, and the 30-day appeal period provided for in § 296 of this title shall be applicable. A notice sent by a corporation or successor entity pursuant to this subsection shall state that any claim rejected therein will be barred if an action, suit or proceeding with respect to the claim is not commenced within 120 days of the date thereof, and shall be accompanied by a copy of §§ 278-283 of this title and, in the case of a notice sent by a court-appointed receiver or trustee and as to which a claim has been filed pursuant to § 295 of this title, copies of §§ 295 and 296 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(3) (src:1474)
`s 280(a)(3) the least time before the end of the period of continuation to mail the rejection` MEANS `period in days` 150

-- src:1474 | (3) A corporation or successor entity may reject, in whole or in part, any claim made by a claimant pursuant to this subsection by mailing notice of such rejection by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to the claimant within 90 days after receipt of such claim and, in all events, at least 150 days before the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title; provided however, that in the case of a claim filed pursuant to § 295 of this title against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery the time period shall be as provided in § 296 of this title, and the 30-day appeal period provided for in § 296 of this title shall be applicable. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(3) (src:1474)
GIVEN `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the claim was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(a)(3) the rejection was mailed in time` MEANS
    IF `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` AT MOST (`the date` `s 280(a)(3) the longest time after receipt of a claim to mail the rejection` `after` `the date the claim was received`)
               AND `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` AT MOST (`the date` `s 280(a)(3) the least time before the end of the period of continuation to mail the rejection` `before` `the last day of the period described in section 278`))

-- "A notice sent by a corporation or successor entity pursuant to this subsection shall state that any claim rejected
-- therein will be barred if an action, suit or proceeding with respect to the claim is not commenced within 120 days
-- of the date thereof, and shall be accompanied by a copy of §§ 278-283 of this title and, in the case of a notice sent
-- by a court-appointed receiver or trustee and as to which a claim has been filed pursuant to § 295 of this title,
-- copies of §§ 295 and 296 of this title." Subsection (g): for a nonstock corporation the notice also includes a copy
-- of section 114.
-- src:1474 | A notice sent by a corporation or successor entity pursuant to this subsection shall state that any claim rejected therein will be barred if an action, suit or proceeding with respect to the claim is not commenced within 120 days of the date thereof, and shall be accompanied by a copy of §§ 278-283 of this title and, in the case of a notice sent by a court-appointed receiver or trustee and as to which a claim has been filed pursuant to § 295 of this title, copies of §§ 295 and 296 of this title.
-- src:1484 | (g) In the case of a nonstock corporation, any notice referred to in the last sentence of paragraph (a)(3) of this section shall include a copy of § 114 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(3) (src:1474), (g) (src:1484)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the notice states that any claim rejected will be barred if an action, suit or proceeding on the claim is not commenced within 120 days of the date of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by a copy of sections 278 to 283` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent by a court-appointed receiver or trustee and a claim has been filed under section 295` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by copies of sections 295 and 296` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by a copy of section 114` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(a)(3) the notice of rejection states and encloses what the paragraph requires` MEANS
        `the notice states that any claim rejected will be barred if an action, suit or proceeding on the claim is not commenced within 120 days of the date of the notice`
    AND `the notice is accompanied by a copy of sections 278 to 283`
    AND ((NOT `the notice is sent by a court-appointed receiver or trustee and a claim has been filed under section 295`) OR `the notice is accompanied by copies of sections 295 and 296`)
    AND ((NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`)) OR `the notice is accompanied by a copy of section 114`)

-- Paragraph (a)(4): "A claim against a corporation is barred if a claimant whose claim is rejected pursuant to paragraph
-- (a)(3) of this section does not commence an action, suit or proceeding with respect to the claim no later than 120
-- days after the mailing of the rejection notice."
-- src:1475 | (4) A claim against a corporation is barred if a claimant whose claim is rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3) of this section does not commence an action, suit or proceeding with respect to the claim no later than 120 days after the mailing of the rejection notice.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(4) (src:1475)
`s 280(a)(4) the longest time after the mailing of the rejection notice to commence an action` MEANS `period in days` 120

@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(a)(4) (src:1475)
GIVEN `the claim was rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the rejection notice was mailed` IS A DATE
      `the date the claimant commenced an action, suit or proceeding on the claim, if the claimant did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(a)(4) the claim is barred for want of an action after the rejection` MEANS
        `the claim was rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3)`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the claimant commenced an action, suit or proceeding on the claim, if the claimant did`
         WHEN JUST commenced THEN commenced GREATER THAN (`the date` `s 280(a)(4) the longest time after the mailing of the rejection notice to commence an action` `after` `the date the rejection notice was mailed`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)

-- Paragraph (b)(1): "contractual claims" excludes "any implied warranty as to any product manufactured, sold, distributed
-- or handled by the dissolved corporation"; the corporation that elects to follow subsection (a) "shall also give
-- notice" to persons with contractual claims contingent, conditional or unmatured, "in substantially the form, and
-- sent and published in the same manner, as described in paragraph (a)(1)".
-- src:1476 | (b) (1) A corporation or successor entity electing to follow the procedures described in subsection (a) of this section shall also give notice of the dissolution of the corporation to persons with contractual claims contingent upon the occurrence or nonoccurrence of future events or otherwise conditional or unmatured, and request that such persons present such claims in accordance with the terms of such notice. Provided however, that as used in this section and in § 281 of this title, the term “contractual claims” shall not include any implied warranty as to any product manufactured, sold, distributed or handled by the dissolved corporation. Such notice shall be in substantially the form, and sent and published in the same manner, as described in paragraph (a)(1) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(b)(1) (src:1476)
GIVEN `the claim is a contractual claim contingent upon the occurrence or nonoccurrence of future events or otherwise conditional or unmatured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is an implied warranty as to a product manufactured, sold, distributed or handled by the dissolved corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(b)(1) the claim is a contractual claim for the purposes of sections 280 and 281` MEANS
        `the claim is a contractual claim contingent upon the occurrence or nonoccurrence of future events or otherwise conditional or unmatured`
    AND (NOT `the claim is an implied warranty as to a product manufactured, sold, distributed or handled by the dissolved corporation`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(b)(1) (src:1476)
GIVEN `the corporation or successor entity elects to follow the procedures described in subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a contractual claim within the meaning of section 280(b)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice to the person is in substantially the form of the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice to the person is sent and published in the same manner as the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(b)(1) the corporation has given the person with a contractual claim the notice it must also give` MEANS
        `the corporation or successor entity elects to follow the procedures described in subsection (a)`
    AND `the person has a contractual claim within the meaning of section 280(b)(1)`
    AND `the notice to the person is in substantially the form of the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)`
    AND `the notice to the person is sent and published in the same manner as the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)`

-- Paragraph (b)(2): the corporation or successor entity offers a claimant on a contract whose claim is contingent,
-- conditional or unmatured "such security as the corporation or successor entity determines is sufficient to provide
-- compensation to the claimant if the claim matures", mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested,
-- "within 90 days of receipt of such claim and, in all events, at least 150 days before the expiration of the period
-- described in § 278".
-- src:1477 | The corporation or successor entity shall mail such offer to the claimant by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, within 90 days of receipt of such claim and, in all events, at least 150 days before the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(b)(2) (src:1477)
GIVEN `the date the contingent claim was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the offer for security was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(b)(2) the offer for security was mailed in time` MEANS
        `the date the offer for security was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` AT MOST (`the date` `s 280(a)(3) the longest time after receipt of a claim to mail the rejection` `after` `the date the contingent claim was received`)
    AND `the date the offer for security was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` AT MOST (`the date` `s 280(a)(3) the least time before the end of the period of continuation to mail the rejection` `before` `the last day of the period described in section 278`)

-- "If the claimant offered such security does not deliver in writing to the corporation or successor entity a notice
-- rejecting the offer within 120 days after receipt of such offer for security, the claimant shall be deemed to have
-- accepted such security as the sole source from which to satisfy the claim against the corporation." The 120th day
-- after receipt is the last day on which the rejection may be delivered (fork F7).
-- src:1477 | If the claimant offered such security does not deliver in writing to the corporation or successor entity a notice rejecting the offer within 120 days after receipt of such offer for security, the claimant shall be deemed to have accepted such security as the sole source from which to satisfy the claim against the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(b)(2) (src:1477)
`s 280(b)(2) the longest time after receipt of the offer to reject it` MEANS `period in days` 120

@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(b)(2) (src:1477)
GIVEN `the date the claimant received the offer for security` IS A DATE
      `the date the claimant delivered in writing a notice rejecting the offer, if the claimant did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(b)(2) the claimant is deemed to have accepted the security as the sole source from which to satisfy the claim` MEANS
        `the date of the question` GREATER THAN `the last day to reject the offer`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the claimant delivered in writing a notice rejecting the offer, if the claimant did`
         WHEN JUST rejected THEN rejected GREATER THAN `the last day to reject the offer`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    WHERE
        `the last day to reject the offer` MEANS `the date` `s 280(b)(2) the longest time after receipt of the offer to reject it` `after` `the date the claimant received the offer for security`

-- Paragraph (c)(1): a corporation or successor entity that has given notice under (a) "shall petition the Court of
-- Chancery to determine the amount and form of security" for a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which
-- the corporation is a party, other than a claim barred under (a).
-- src:1478 | (c) (1) A corporation or successor entity which has given notice in accordance with subsection (a) of this section shall petition the Court of Chancery to determine the amount and form of security that will be reasonably likely to be sufficient to provide compensation for any claim against the corporation which is the subject of a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party other than a claim barred pursuant to subsection (a) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(c)(1) (src:1478)
GIVEN `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is the subject of a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is barred pursuant to subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(c)(1) the corporation or successor entity must petition the Court of Chancery to determine the security for the pending claim` MEANS
        `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsection (a)`
    AND `the claim is the subject of a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party`
    AND (NOT `the claim is barred pursuant to subsection (a)`)

-- Paragraph (c)(2): after notice under (a) and (b), a petition "to determine the amount and form of security that will be
-- sufficient to provide compensation to any claimant who has rejected the offer for security made pursuant to
-- paragraph (b)(2)".
-- src:1479 | (2) A corporation or successor entity which has given notice in accordance with subsections (a) and (b) of this section shall petition the Court of Chancery to determine the amount and form of security that will be sufficient to provide compensation to any claimant who has rejected the offer for security made pursuant to paragraph (b)(2) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(c)(2) (src:1479)
GIVEN `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsections (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has rejected the offer for security made pursuant to paragraph (b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(c)(2) the corporation or successor entity must petition the Court of Chancery to determine the security for the claimant who rejected the offer` MEANS
        `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsections (a) and (b)`
    AND `the claimant has rejected the offer for security made pursuant to paragraph (b)(2)`

-- Paragraph (c)(3): claims "likely to arise or to become known ... within 5 years after the date of dissolution or such
-- longer period of time as the Court of Chancery may determine not to exceed 10 years after the date of dissolution".
-- A longer period beyond 10 years is not one the text allows: NOTHING.
-- src:1480 | (3) A corporation or successor entity which has given notice in accordance with subsection (a) of this section shall petition the Court of Chancery to determine the amount and form of security which will be reasonably likely to be sufficient to provide compensation for claims that have not been made known to the corporation or that have not arisen but that, based on facts known to the corporation or successor entity, are likely to arise or to become known to the corporation or successor entity within 5 years after the date of dissolution or such longer period of time as the Court of Chancery may determine not to exceed 10 years after the date of dissolution. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(c)(3) (src:1480)
GIVEN `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(c)(3) the corporation or successor entity must petition the Court of Chancery to determine the security for claims not yet made known` MEANS
    `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsection (a)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(c)(3) (src:1480)
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 280(c)(3) the last day of the period within which claims likely to arise are provided for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the end of the 5 years`
    WHEN JUST longer THEN
        IF longer GREATER THAN `the end of the 10 years`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (IF longer GREATER THAN `the end of the 5 years` THEN longer ELSE `the end of the 5 years`)
    WHERE
        `the end of the 5 years` MEANS `the date` (`period in years` 5) `after` `the date of dissolution`
        `the end of the 10 years` MEANS `the date` (`period in years` 10) `after` `the date of dissolution`

-- "The Court of Chancery may appoint a guardian ad litem in respect of any such proceeding brought under this
-- subsection. The reasonable fees and expenses of such guardian, including all reasonable expert witness fees, shall be
-- paid by the petitioner in such proceeding." Where no guardian is appointed the sentence says nothing.
-- src:1480 | The Court of Chancery may appoint a guardian ad litem in respect of any such proceeding brought under this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(c)(3) (src:1480)
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery has appointed a guardian ad litem in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(c)(3) the reasonable fees and expenses of the guardian ad litem are paid by the petitioner` MEANS
    IF `the Court of Chancery has appointed a guardian ad litem in the proceeding` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (d): "The giving of any notice or making of any offer pursuant to this section shall not revive any claim
-- then barred or constitute acknowledgment by the corporation or successor entity that any person to whom such
-- notice is sent is a proper claimant and shall not operate as a waiver of any defense or counterclaim".
-- src:1481 | (d) The giving of any notice or making of any offer pursuant to this section shall not revive any claim then barred or constitute acknowledgment by the corporation or successor entity that any person to whom such notice is sent is a proper claimant and shall not operate as a waiver of any defense or counterclaim in respect of any claim asserted by any person to whom such notice is sent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(d) (src:1481)
DECLARE `s 280(d) Effect of giving a notice or making an offer` IS ONE OF
    `it revives a claim then barred`
    `it is an acknowledgment that the person to whom it is sent is a proper claimant`
    `it operates as a waiver of a defense or counterclaim in respect of a claim`

-- src:1481 | (d) The giving of any notice or making of any offer pursuant to this section shall not revive any claim then barred or constitute acknowledgment by the corporation or successor entity that any person to whom such notice is sent is a proper claimant and shall not operate as a waiver of any defense or counterclaim in respect of any claim asserted by any person to whom such notice is sent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(d) (src:1481)
GIVEN `the effect` IS A `s 280(d) Effect of giving a notice or making an offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(d) the giving of the notice or the making of the offer has the effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the effect`
    WHEN `it revives a claim then barred` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `it is an acknowledgment that the person to whom it is sent is a proper claimant` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `it operates as a waiver of a defense or counterclaim in respect of a claim` THEN FALSE

-- Subsection (e): "the term 'successor entity' shall include any trust, receivership or other legal entity governed
-- by the laws of this State to which the remaining assets and liabilities of a dissolved corporation are transferred
-- and which exists solely for the purposes of prosecuting and defending suits ... but not for the purpose of continuing
-- the business". "Include" is not exhaustive: an entity that does not meet the description is not said to be outside the
-- term, so that case answers NOTHING.
-- src:1482 | (e) As used in this section, the term “successor entity” shall include any trust, receivership or other legal entity governed by the laws of this State to which the remaining assets and liabilities of a dissolved corporation are transferred and which exists solely for the purposes of prosecuting and defending suits, by or against the dissolved corporation, enabling the dissolved corporation to settle and close the business of the dissolved corporation, to dispose of and convey the property of the dissolved corporation, to discharge the liabilities of the dissolved corporation and to distribute to the dissolved corporation’s stockholders any remaining assets, but not for the purpose of continuing the business for which the dissolved corporation was organized.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(e) (src:1482)
GIVEN `the entity is a trust, receivership or other legal entity governed by the laws of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remaining assets and liabilities of the dissolved corporation are transferred to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it exists solely for the purposes of prosecuting and defending suits, enabling the dissolved corporation to settle and close its business, disposing of and conveying its property, discharging its liabilities and distributing any remaining assets to its stockholders, but not for the purpose of continuing the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(e) the entity is a successor entity` MEANS
    IF     `the entity is a trust, receivership or other legal entity governed by the laws of this State`
       AND `the remaining assets and liabilities of the dissolved corporation are transferred to it`
       AND `it exists solely for the purposes of prosecuting and defending suits, enabling the dissolved corporation to settle and close its business, disposing of and conveying its property, discharging its liabilities and distributing any remaining assets to its stockholders, but not for the purpose of continuing the business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (f): where the Court of Chancery has appointed a receiver or trustee, "the time periods and notice
-- requirements of this section shall ... be subject to variation by, or in the manner provided in, the Rules of the Court
-- of Chancery" (not among the inputs). Where they are varied the section's own figures are not the answer: NOTHING.
-- src:1483 | (f) The time periods and notice requirements of this section shall, in the case of a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery, be subject to variation by, or in the manner provided in, the Rules of the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(f) (src:1483)
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery has appointed a receiver or trustee for the corporation or successor entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Rules of the Court of Chancery vary the time period or notice requirement` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Rules of the Court of Chancery are not among the inputs
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(f) the time periods and notice requirements of the section apply as the section states them` MEANS
    IF     `the Court of Chancery has appointed a receiver or trustee for the corporation or successor entity`
       AND `the Rules of the Court of Chancery vary the time period or notice requirement`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (g), second sentence: "In the case of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, provisions of this section regarding
-- distributions to members shall not apply to the extent that those provisions conflict with any other applicable law or
-- with that corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws."
-- src:1484 | In the case of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, provisions of this section regarding distributions to members shall not apply to the extent that those provisions conflict with any other applicable law or with that corporation’s certificate of incorporation or bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 280(g) (src:1484)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the provisions of section 280 regarding distributions to members conflict with other applicable law or with the corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(g) the provisions of section 280 regarding distributions to members apply` MEANS
    NOT (        `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
             AND `the provisions of section 280 regarding distributions to members conflict with other applicable law or with the corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws`)

§§ `s 281 Payment and distribution to claimants and stockholders`

-- Subsection (a): a dissolved corporation or successor entity that has followed the section 280 procedures (1) shall pay
-- the claims made and not rejected in accordance with 280(a), (2) shall post the security offered and not rejected under
-- 280(b)(2), (3) shall post any security ordered by the Court under 280(c), and (4) shall pay or make provision for all
-- other claims that are mature, known and uncontested or that have been finally determined to be owing.
-- src:1488 | (a) A dissolved corporation or successor entity which has followed the procedures described in § 280 of this title:
-- src:1489 | (1) Shall pay the claims made and not rejected in accordance with § 280(a) of this title,
-- src:1490 | (2) Shall post the security offered and not rejected pursuant to § 280(b)(2) of this title,
-- src:1491 | (3) Shall post any security ordered by the Court of Chancery in any proceeding under § 280(c) of this title, and
-- src:1492 | (4) Shall pay or make provision for all other claims that are mature, known and uncontested or that have been finally determined to be owing by the corporation or such successor entity.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(a) (src:1488-1492)
GIVEN `the corporation or successor entity has followed the procedures described in section 280` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made and not rejected in accordance with section 280(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `security was offered and not rejected pursuant to section 280(b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `security was ordered by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under section 280(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is mature, known and uncontested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim has been finally determined to be owing by the corporation or successor entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 281(a) the corporation or successor entity must pay the claim or post the security` MEANS
        `the corporation or successor entity has followed the procedures described in section 280`
    AND (    `the claim was made and not rejected in accordance with section 280(a)`
         OR  `security was offered and not rejected pursuant to section 280(b)(2)`
         OR  `security was ordered by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under section 280(c)`
         OR  `the claim is mature, known and uncontested`
         OR  `the claim has been finally determined to be owing by the corporation or successor entity`)

-- "Such claims or obligations shall be paid in full and any such provision for payment shall be made in full if there are
-- sufficient assets. If there are insufficient assets, such claims and obligations shall be paid or provided for according
-- to their priority, and, among claims of equal priority, ratably to the extent of assets legally available therefor."
-- The rule is for one class of claims of equal priority; the assets left for the class are the caller's figure
-- (priority itself is not defined by the text, subsection (e)). A claim above its class or a class of nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:1493 | Such claims or obligations shall be paid in full and any such provision for payment shall be made in full if there are sufficient assets. If there are insufficient assets, such claims and obligations shall be paid or provided for according to their priority, and, among claims of equal priority, ratably to the extent of assets legally available therefor. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(a) (src:1493)
GIVEN `the amount of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the claims of equal priority` IS A NUMBER
      `the assets legally available for the claims of that priority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 281(a) the amount paid or provided for on the claim` MEANS
    IF     `the total of the claims of equal priority` GREATER THAN 0
       AND `the amount of the claim` AT LEAST 0
       AND `the amount of the claim` AT MOST `the total of the claims of equal priority`
       AND `the assets legally available for the claims of that priority` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST (IF `the assets legally available for the claims of that priority` AT LEAST `the total of the claims of equal priority`
               THEN `the amount of the claim`
               ELSE `the amount of the claim` TIMES (`the assets legally available for the claims of that priority` DIVIDED BY `the total of the claims of equal priority`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Any remaining assets shall be distributed to the stockholders of the dissolved corporation; provided, however, that
-- such distribution shall not be made before the expiration of 150 days from the date of the last notice of rejections
-- given pursuant to § 280(a)(3) of this title." Reading taken (fork F8): the distribution may be made on the day after the
-- 150th day. With no notice of rejection the proviso has nothing to run from: NOTHING.
-- src:1493 | Any remaining assets shall be distributed to the stockholders of the dissolved corporation; provided, however, that such distribution shall not be made before the expiration of 150 days from the date of the last notice of rejections given pursuant to § 280(a)(3) of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(a) (src:1493)
`s 281(a) the time to wait after the last notice of rejections before distributing to the stockholders` MEANS `period in days` 150

@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(a) (src:1493)
GIVEN `the date of the proposed distribution to the stockholders` IS A DATE
      `the date of the last notice of rejections given pursuant to section 280(a)(3), if any was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(a) the distribution to the stockholders may be made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of the last notice of rejections given pursuant to section 280(a)(3), if any was given`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the date of the proposed distribution to the stockholders` GREATER THAN (`the date` `s 281(a) the time to wait after the last notice of rejections before distributing to the stockholders` `after` last))

-- "In the absence of actual fraud, the judgment of the directors of the dissolved corporation or the governing persons of
-- such successor entity as to the provision made for the payment of all obligations under paragraph (a)(4) of this
-- section shall be conclusive." Where there was actual fraud the sentence says nothing.
-- src:1493 | In the absence of actual fraud, the judgment of the directors of the dissolved corporation or the governing persons of such successor entity as to the provision made for the payment of all obligations under paragraph (a)(4) of this section shall be conclusive.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(a) (src:1493)
GIVEN `there was actual fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(a) the judgment of the directors or governing persons as to the provision for obligations under paragraph (a)(4) is conclusive` MEANS
    IF `there was actual fraud` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (b): a dissolved corporation or successor entity that has not followed section 280 shall, "prior to the
-- expiration of the period described in § 278", adopt a plan of distribution which (i) pays or makes reasonable
-- provision for all claims and obligations, including known contingent, conditional or unmatured contractual claims,
-- (ii) makes provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for pending actions, and (iii) makes such provision for claims
-- likely to arise within 10 years after dissolution; pays in full if the assets suffice, otherwise by priority and ratably;
-- and distributes any remaining assets to the stockholders.
-- src:1494 | (b) A dissolved corporation or successor entity which has not followed the procedures described in § 280 of this title shall, prior to the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title, adopt a plan of distribution pursuant to which the dissolved corporation or successor entity (i) shall pay or make reasonable provision to pay all claims and obligations, including all contingent, conditional or unmatured contractual claims known to the corporation or such successor entity, (ii) shall make such provision as will be reasonably likely to be sufficient to provide compensation for any claim against the corporation which is the subject of a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party and (iii) shall make such provision as will be reasonably likely to be sufficient to provide compensation for claims that have not been made known to the corporation or that have not arisen but that, based on facts known to the corporation or successor entity, are likely to arise or to become known to the corporation or successor entity within 10 years after the date of dissolution. The plan of distribution shall provide that such claims shall be paid in full and any such provision for payment made shall be made in full if there are sufficient assets. If there are insufficient assets, such plan shall provide that such claims and obligations shall be paid or provided for according to their priority and, among claims of equal priority, ratably to the extent of assets legally available therefor. Any remaining assets shall be distributed to the stockholders of the dissolved corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(b) (src:1494)
DECLARE `s 281(b) Plan of distribution` HAS
    `provision to pay or make reasonable provision to pay all claims and obligations, including known contingent, conditional or unmatured contractual claims` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for claims in pending actions, suits or proceedings to which the corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for claims likely to arise or become known within 10 years after the date of dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision that the claims be paid in full if there are sufficient assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision that, if the assets are insufficient, the claims be paid according to their priority and, among claims of equal priority, ratably` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision that any remaining assets be distributed to the stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1494 | (b) A dissolved corporation or successor entity which has not followed the procedures described in § 280 of this title shall, prior to the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title, adopt a plan of distribution pursuant to which the dissolved corporation or successor entity (i) shall pay or make reasonable provision to pay all claims and obligations, including all contingent, conditional or unmatured contractual claims known to the corporation or such successor entity, (ii) shall make such provision as will be reasonably likely to be sufficient to provide compensation for any claim against the corporation which is the subject of a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party and (iii) shall make such provision as will be reasonably likely to be sufficient to provide compensation for claims that have not been made known to the corporation or that have not arisen but that, based on facts known to the corporation or successor entity, are likely to arise or to become known to the corporation or successor entity within 10 years after the date of dissolution. The plan of distribution shall provide that such claims shall be paid in full and any such provision for payment made shall be made in full if there are sufficient assets. If there are insufficient assets, such plan shall provide that such claims and obligations shall be paid or provided for according to their priority and, among claims of equal priority, ratably to the extent of assets legally available therefor. Any remaining assets shall be distributed to the stockholders of the dissolved corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(b) (src:1494)
GIVEN `the plan` IS A `s 281(b) Plan of distribution`
      `the date the plan of distribution was adopted` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 281(b) the plan of distribution was adopted in time and provides what the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the date the plan of distribution was adopted` AT MOST `the last day of the period described in section 278`
    AND `the plan`'s `provision to pay or make reasonable provision to pay all claims and obligations, including known contingent, conditional or unmatured contractual claims`
    AND `the plan`'s `provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for claims in pending actions, suits or proceedings to which the corporation is a party`
    AND `the plan`'s `provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for claims likely to arise or become known within 10 years after the date of dissolution`
    AND `the plan`'s `provision that the claims be paid in full if there are sufficient assets`
    AND `the plan`'s `provision that, if the assets are insufficient, the claims be paid according to their priority and, among claims of equal priority, ratably`
    AND `the plan`'s `provision that any remaining assets be distributed to the stockholders`

-- Subsection (c): "Directors of a dissolved corporation or governing persons of a successor entity which has complied
-- with subsection (a) or (b) of this section shall not be personally liable to the claimants of the dissolved corporation."
-- Where neither is complied with the subsection gives no protection and says nothing of liability: NOTHING.
-- src:1495 | (c) Directors of a dissolved corporation or governing persons of a successor entity which has complied with subsection (a) or (b) of this section shall not be personally liable to the claimants of the dissolved corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(c) (src:1495)
GIVEN `the corporation or successor entity has complied with subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or successor entity has complied with subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(c) the directors or governing persons are not personally liable to the claimants` MEANS
    IF `the corporation or successor entity has complied with subsection (a)` OR `the corporation or successor entity has complied with subsection (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (e): "The term 'priority,' as used in this section, does not refer either to the order of payments set forth
-- in paragraph (a)(1)-(4) of this section or to the relative times at which any claims mature or are reduced to
-- judgment." The text says only what priority is not.
-- src:1497 | (e) The term “priority,” as used in this section, does not refer either to the order of payments set forth in paragraph (a)(1)-(4) of this section or to the relative times at which any claims mature or are reduced to judgment.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(e) (src:1497)
DECLARE `s 281(e) Ground for ranking claims` IS ONE OF
    `the order of payments set forth in paragraph (a)(1) to (4)`
    `the relative times at which claims mature`
    `the relative times at which claims are reduced to judgment`
    `any other ground for ranking claims`

-- src:1497 | (e) The term “priority,” as used in this section, does not refer either to the order of payments set forth in paragraph (a)(1)-(4) of this section or to the relative times at which any claims mature or are reduced to judgment.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(e) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `s 281(e) Ground for ranking claims`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(e) the ground is what the term priority refers to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `any other ground for ranking claims` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- Subsection (f): the same carve-out for a nonprofit nonstock corporation as in section 280(g).
-- src:1498 | (f) In the case of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, provisions of this section regarding distributions to members shall not apply to the extent that those provisions conflict with any other applicable law or with that corporation’s certificate of incorporation or bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 281(f) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the provisions of section 281 regarding distributions to members conflict with other applicable law or with the corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 281(f) the provisions of section 281 regarding distributions to members apply` MEANS
    NOT (        `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
             AND `the provisions of section 281 regarding distributions to members conflict with other applicable law or with the corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws`)

§§ `s 282 Liability of stockholders of dissolved corporations`

-- Subsection (a): "A stockholder of a dissolved corporation the assets of which were distributed pursuant to § 281(a) or
-- (b) of this title shall not be liable for any claim against the corporation in an amount in excess of such
-- stockholder's pro rata share of the claim or the amount so distributed to such stockholder, whichever is less."
-- The pro rata share is the caller's figure; the section does not compute it.
-- src:1502 | (a) A stockholder of a dissolved corporation the assets of which were distributed pursuant to § 281(a) or (b) of this title shall not be liable for any claim against the corporation in an amount in excess of such stockholder’s pro rata share of the claim or the amount so distributed to such stockholder, whichever is less.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 282(a) (src:1502)
GIVEN `the assets of the dissolved corporation were distributed pursuant to section 281(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder's pro rata share of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount distributed to the stockholder` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 282(a) the most the stockholder is liable for on the claim` MEANS
    IF `the assets of the dissolved corporation were distributed pursuant to section 281(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST (min `the stockholder's pro rata share of the claim` `the amount distributed to the stockholder`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (b): "A stockholder of a dissolved corporation the assets of which were distributed pursuant to § 281(a) of
-- this title shall not be liable for any claim against the corporation on which an action, suit or proceeding is not
-- begun prior to the expiration of the period described in § 278". It is for a distribution under 281(a) only, not (b).
-- Where the action was begun in time, or the distribution was under 281(b), the subsection says nothing.
-- src:1503 | (b) A stockholder of a dissolved corporation the assets of which were distributed pursuant to § 281(a) of this title shall not be liable for any claim against the corporation on which an action, suit or proceeding is not begun prior to the expiration of the period described in § 278 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 282(b) (src:1503)
GIVEN `the assets of the dissolved corporation were distributed pursuant to section 281(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an action, suit or proceeding on the claim was begun prior to the expiration of the period described in section 278` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282(b) the stockholder is not liable for the claim` MEANS
    IF `the assets of the dissolved corporation were distributed pursuant to section 281(a)` AND (NOT `an action, suit or proceeding on the claim was begun prior to the expiration of the period described in section 278`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (c): "The aggregate liability of any stockholder of a dissolved corporation for claims against the dissolved
-- corporation shall not exceed the amount distributed to such stockholder in dissolution."
-- src:1504 | (c) The aggregate liability of any stockholder of a dissolved corporation for claims against the dissolved corporation shall not exceed the amount distributed to such stockholder in dissolution.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 282(c) (src:1504)
GIVEN `the amounts for which the stockholder is liable on each claim` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the amount distributed to the stockholder in dissolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 282(c) the most the stockholder is liable for on all the claims together` MEANS
    min (sum `the amounts for which the stockholder is liable on each claim`) `the amount distributed to the stockholder in dissolution`

§§ `s 283 Jurisdiction`

-- "The Court of Chancery shall have jurisdiction of any application prescribed in this subchapter and of all questions
-- arising in the proceedings thereon, and may make such orders and decrees and issue injunctions therein as justice and
-- equity shall require."
-- src:1508 | The Court of Chancery shall have jurisdiction of any application prescribed in this subchapter and of all questions arising in the proceedings thereon, and may make such orders and decrees and issue injunctions therein as justice and equity shall require.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 283 (src:1508)
GIVEN `the application is one prescribed in Subchapter X, sections 271 to 285` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 283 the Court of Chancery has jurisdiction of the application and may make the orders, decrees and injunctions justice and equity require` MEANS
    `the application is one prescribed in Subchapter X, sections 271 to 285`

§§ `s 284 Revocation or forfeiture of charter; proceedings`

-- Subsection (a): "Upon motion by the Attorney General, the Court of Chancery shall have jurisdiction to revoke or forfeit
-- the charter of any corporation for abuse, misuse or nonuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises. The
-- Attorney General shall proceed for this purpose by complaint in the Court of Chancery."
-- src:1512 | (a) Upon motion by the Attorney General, the Court of Chancery shall have jurisdiction to revoke or forfeit the charter of any corporation for abuse, misuse or nonuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises. The Attorney General shall proceed for this purpose by complaint in the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 284(a) (src:1512)
DECLARE `s 284(a) Ground for revoking or forfeiting the charter` IS ONE OF
    `abuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises`
    `misuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises`
    `nonuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises`

-- Subsection (c): "No proceeding shall be instituted under this section for nonuse of any corporation's powers,
-- privileges or franchises during the first 2 years after its incorporation." Reading taken (fork F9): the first 2 years end
-- on the day before the second anniversary of incorporation, so a proceeding may be instituted on the anniversary itself.
-- src:1514 | (c) No proceeding shall be instituted under this section for nonuse of any corporation’s powers, privileges or franchises during the first 2 years after its incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 284(c) (src:1514)
`s 284(c) the time after incorporation during which no proceeding for nonuse is instituted` MEANS `period in years` 2

-- src:1512 | (a) Upon motion by the Attorney General, the Court of Chancery shall have jurisdiction to revoke or forfeit the charter of any corporation for abuse, misuse or nonuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises. The Attorney General shall proceed for this purpose by complaint in the Court of Chancery.
-- src:1514 | (c) No proceeding shall be instituted under this section for nonuse of any corporation’s powers, privileges or franchises during the first 2 years after its incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 284(a) (src:1512), (c) (src:1514)
GIVEN `the Attorney General proceeds by complaint in the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground` IS A `s 284(a) Ground for revoking or forfeiting the charter`
      `the date the corporation was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the date the proceeding is instituted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 284 a proceeding to revoke or forfeit the charter may be instituted` MEANS
        `the Attorney General proceeds by complaint in the Court of Chancery`
    AND (CONSIDER `the ground`
         WHEN `nonuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises` THEN `the date the proceeding is instituted` AT LEAST (`the date` `s 284(c) the time after incorporation during which no proceeding for nonuse is instituted` `after` `the date the corporation was incorporated`)
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- Subsection (b): "The Court of Chancery shall have power, by appointment of trustees, receivers or otherwise, to
-- administer and wind up the affairs of any corporation whose charter shall be revoked or forfeited by the Court of
-- Chancery under this section, and to make such orders and decrees with respect thereto as shall be just and equitable
-- respecting its affairs and assets and the rights of its stockholders and creditors."
-- src:1513 | (b) The Court of Chancery shall have power, by appointment of trustees, receivers or otherwise, to administer and wind up the affairs of any corporation whose charter shall be revoked or forfeited by the Court of Chancery under this section, and to make such orders and decrees with respect thereto as shall be just and equitable respecting its affairs and assets and the rights of its stockholders and creditors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 284(b) (src:1513)
GIVEN `the charter of the corporation has been revoked or forfeited by the Court of Chancery under section 284` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 284(b) the Court of Chancery has power to administer and wind up the affairs of the corporation and to make the orders and decrees just and equitable respecting its affairs and assets and the rights of its stockholders and creditors` MEANS
    `the charter of the corporation has been revoked or forfeited by the Court of Chancery under section 284`

§§ `s 285 Dissolution or forfeiture of charter by decree of court; filing`

-- "Whenever any corporation is dissolved or its charter forfeited by decree or judgment of the Court of Chancery, the
-- decree or judgment shall be forthwith filed by the Register in Chancery of the county in which the decree or judgment
-- was entered, in the office of the Secretary of State, and a note thereof shall be made by the Secretary of State on the
-- corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation and on the index thereof."
-- src:1518 | Whenever any corporation is dissolved or its charter forfeited by decree or judgment of the Court of Chancery, the decree or judgment shall be forthwith filed by the Register in Chancery of the county in which the decree or judgment was entered, in the office of the Secretary of State, and a note thereof shall be made by the Secretary of State on the corporation’s charter or certificate of incorporation and on the index thereof.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 285 (src:1518)
GIVEN `the corporation has been dissolved or its charter forfeited by decree or judgment of the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 285 the decree or judgment must be filed in the office of the Secretary of State and noted on the charter and the index` MEANS
    `the corporation has been dissolved or its charter forfeited by decree or judgment of the Court of Chancery`
